 ],
 "note": "SA74 night stage FSS3, refixed 01:46 PST before any of its runs (replaces the 01:44 version, sha b06bde97, which never ran): replicas for the small-grid end of the finite-size series, now also at Hamber's k_c. The night chains show autocorrelation times of 100 to 300 sweeps at every size, so single chains give effective sample sizes of 10 to 40. Flat starts at L = 3, 4, 6: four chains at k = 0.245 (beside Hamber's k_c = 0.2443, where he fits the curvature against size) and three more at each of k = 0.2475 and 0.2525 (beside the FSS2 chain), a = 0.005, ten rescalings per sweep, the FSS2 lengths. Purpose: the curvature and its fluctuation against L at fixed k with chain-to-chain errors."
